Let's understand the meanings of the parts of this equation.

$\begin{align}
\boxed{\begin{align}
\scriptsize\text{Proportion of}&\quad\qquad\scriptsize\text{Number of milliliters}
\\
\scriptsize\text{butterfat}&\quad\qquad\scriptsize\text{of whipping cream}
\\
&\searrow\quad\qquad\swarrow
\\
&\large \underbrace{\overbrace{0.18}\cdot\overbrace{x}}
\\
&\qquad\uparrow
\\
&\scriptsize\text{Volume of butterfat in whipping cream}
\end{align}}
\\\\
\boxed{\begin{align}
\scriptsize\text{Proportion of}&\quad\qquad\scriptsize\text{Number of milliliters}
\\
\scriptsize\text{butterfat}&\quad\qquad\scriptsize\text{of milk}
\\
&\searrow\quad\qquad\swarrow
\\
&\large \underbrace{\overbrace{0.04}\cdot\overbrace{y}}
\\
&\qquad\uparrow
\\
&\scriptsize\text{Volume of butterfat in milk}
\end{align}}
\end{align}$

So $0.18x+0.04y$ is the total milliliters of butterfat in both liquids, and we want that to be equal to $0.12(500)$, which is $12\%$ of the total $500\,\text{mL}$ of the mixture.
